    {
      "title": "'All this food is now useless': Piles of rubbish after shop freezers hit by cyber-attack",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cmwyvrgk9p0ro?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "Dozens of supermarkets in seven European countries dumped huge quantities of food after refrigerators and freezers were targeted in a cyber-attack.",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-11-02T17:34:58"
    },
    {
      "title": "If hackers can take control of a supermarket freezer, how vulnerable is other tech?",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckpqg8lve73go?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "Dozens of shops across European countries have been hit by a cyber-attack affecting their fridges.",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-11-02T18:25:01"
    },
    {
      "title": "Who is hacking Europe’s supermarket fridges and freezers, and why?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/02/europe-supermarket-fridges-freezers-who-hacking-why",
      "description": "<p>After a second apparent cyber-attack in as many weeks, we examine possible culprits and their motives</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/supermarket-freezers-across-europe-hit-by-second-suspected-cyber-attack\">Shop fridges and freezers across Europe hit by fresh suspected cyber-attack</a></p></li></ul><p>Supermarket fridges and freezers in seven European countries <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/supermarket-freezers-across-europe-hit-by-second-suspected-cyber-attack\">have malfunctioned</a>, their thermostats remotely cranked up in some cases to 50C (122F).</p><p>The EU has condemned what it said was “a deliberate attempt to disrupt our food supply chain and undermine consumers’ confidence in it”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/02/europe-supermarket-fridges-freezers-who-hacking-why\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T19:07:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "Shop fridges and freezers across Europe hit by fresh suspected cyber-attack",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/supermarket-freezers-across-europe-hit-by-second-suspected-cyber-attack",
      "description": "<p>Chains in seven countries say cooling unit temperatures rose overnight in incident similar to hack of French shops</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/02/europe-supermarket-fridges-freezers-who-hacking-why\">Who is hacking Europe’s supermarket fridges and freezers, and why?</a></p></li></ul><p>Supermarket chains in at least seven European countries have said the temperatures of refrigerators and freezers in some of their shops soared overnight to as high as 50C (122F), echoing a cyber-attack last month that caused millions of euros of damage in France.</p><p>Retailers in Belgium, Estonia, Ireland, Finland, Luxembourg, the Netherlands and Sweden reported problems with their refrigeration systems on Monday, and several companies confirmed they had been hacked.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/supermarket-freezers-across-europe-hit-by-second-suspected-cyber-attack\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T16:39:20"
    }
  ]
